cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Threadfin: clone-level analysis of B-cell states from paired single-cell RNA-seq and BCR-seq"
message: "If you use Threadfin, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Satoshi
    given-names: Chen
    alias: Reynold4k
url: "https://github.com/Reynold4k/Threadfin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Reynold4k/Threadfin"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23824521
license: MIT
version: 4.6.1
date-released: "2026-10-31"
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - scRNA-seq
  - BCR
  - B cell
  - clonal lineage
  - germinal centre
  - immunology
abstract: >-
  Threadfin infers relationships between B-cell clones from paired
  single-cell RNA and B-cell receptor sequencing. Each clone defined by its
  receptor is represented by the distribution of transcriptional states among
  its sampled cells, estimated relative to cells from the same individual or
  sample and shrunk according to the number of cells sampled. Clones are
  compared in a clone embedding, whose layout is chosen for each dataset so
  that continuous populations of clones remain connected, in clonal
  programmes, and with permutation tests that respect the sampling design.
